repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab9"
abstract: >-
  Donghyuncr is a browser-based, noncommercial side-scrolling action
  platformer for one player. The number of lives (0 = invincible), the starting
  form and the starting stage are chosen only through programs written in the
  esoteric programming language Donghyun-lang; the three stages themselves are
  played with the keyboard, with a Bluetooth or USB gamepad through the
  browser Gamepad API (Nintendo layout: A = X key jump, B = Z key attack, Y =
  A key info, d-pad or left stick = left/right, + = Enter), or with on-screen
  buttons, using the same key layout as Donghyunjeon and Donghyunwar. Stages
  are played in sequence (score carried over, lives refilled), transformation
  badges placed in every stage change the hero's form (there is no transform
  button; losing a life returns the hero to the starting form), and the third
  stage ends with a boss fight against the Neotank of
  Donghyunjeon. The hero is Podong-i, the author's dog; enemies and
  transformations are borrowed from the other Donghyun laboratories. Its
  overall structure (run-and-jump stages, switchable forms) is inspired by the
  Game Boy game Crayon Shin-chan 4 (1996); it contains none of that game's
  graphics, sound, level layouts, text or characters, and omits its arcade
  mini-games. Crayon Shin-chan is the work of Yoshito Usui and Futabasha; this
  work is not affiliated with or endorsed by them or Bandai. The MIT license
  applies to the application code, documentation and original artwork only;
  the fonts are under the SIL Open Font License, and the name and likeness of
  Podong-i remain with the author. See LICENSE and CREDITS.md.
keywords:
  - platform game
  - pixel art
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
  - gamepad
